---
description: Supabase function or view creation or update
alwaysApply: false
---

When creating a Supabase function, always use SECURITY INVOKER. Unless explicitly stated otherwise, users should access rows and tables only if they have the proper RLS permissions. Never create a function with SECURITY DEFINER.

Example:


CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.say_hello(name text)
RETURNS text
LANGUAGE plpgsql
SECURITY INVOKER
AS $$
BEGIN
RETURN 'Hello ' || name;
END;
$$;


Example for views


CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW public.my_view
WITH (security_invoker = true) AS
SELECT …;
